  "about": {
    "title": "About Visual Routines",
    "description": "Executive functions are cognitive processes that help us plan, focus attention, remember instructions, and manage multiple tasks successfully. For children, especially those with autism or ADHD, these skills can be challenging. Visual routines—such as step-by-step picture schedules or illustrated checklists—support executive functioning by providing clear, predictable guidance. They reduce cognitive load, help with task initiation and completion, and promote independence by making abstract concepts like time, order, and priorities more concrete and accessible.",
    "feature1": "Visual activity cards kids can understand",
    "feature2": "Explore templates to get started",
    "feature3": "Daily auto-reset for recurring routines",
    "feature4": "Export routines as printable PDFs",
    "feature5": "Works offline on any device",
    "madeWith": "Made with ❤️ for parents and kids"
